WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.590
You've heard of a girl named Lain, right?

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.830
Lain of the Wired.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.960
Are your parents away on vacation or something?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.390
I called the number you gave me, but no one answered.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.220
I'm not lying.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.230
No, I don't think you're lying. I checked.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.970
You're Iwakura Lain, all right.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.230
Your address and phone number check out.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.380
It's late, so I'm going to have someone take you home.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.210
But next time, I want you to talk to me.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.910
Keeping quiet is a bad idea, even if you weren't involved.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.740
For crying out loud...

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.920
Lain, I'm sorry!

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.810
This is all our fault. Are you okay, Lain?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.330
Are you all right, Lain?

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.260
A...

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.260
What is it, Lain?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.270
A... ri... su.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.070
Arisu! Come on! We're going home.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.780
Lain...

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.250
Arisu!

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.550
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry, Lain...

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.120
Tomorrow... Let's talk tomorrow, okay?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.370
I'm sorry!

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.850
So do you want to head home, too?

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.380
A... risu.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.690
You have a key, right?

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.620
Yes.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.910
Message...

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.890
There are no messages for Lain.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.200
Good night, Navi.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.600
Good night, Lain.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:59.040
Don't you think it's embarrassing for a junior high-schooler

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.900
to oversleep and be late for school?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:06.790
Mom, about last night...

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.960
Hm? What about it?

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.460
Never mind.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.190
Lain.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:05.970
Lain.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.330
Lain.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:16.070
It's me, Lain. You can hear me, can't you?

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.780
Who's there?

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.870
You are not alone.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:29.500
'Morning!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.860
Good morning!

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.630
Oh, my god!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.700
Was he cute?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.430
Yeah, they wouldn't show his face on TV!

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:41.310
Well...

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.640
Oh, you were screaming the whole time. Did you even see his face?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.600
Well, yeah, but...

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.250
I was a little...

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.810
You were too scared to look.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.060
Lain!

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.430
Lain, did you get in trouble yesterday?

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.860
Come on, it wasn't really our fault.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.280
I'm sorry. I'll be right back.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:06.530
Right, Arisu was closest to the guy!

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.690
So, was there blood splattered all over?

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.070
Yeah...

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:12.770
Tell them!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:13.290
Come on!

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.640
Arisu!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:22.010
But that's not all.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:28.010
If you look at the Psyche as a mere processor, you lose sight of the whole.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.690
As a multi-purpose information terminal,

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.630
the Navi has come into wide use even among grade-schoolers.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:39.070
However, activity within the Wired is currently limited by the machine.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.400
The Psyche can dramatically increase the performance of any Navi.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.430
There was no reason for me to stay in the real world any longer.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:55.200
In the real world, it didn't matter if I was there or not.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:11:02.910
When I realized that, I was no longer afraid of losing my body.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:05.890
Who is Lain?

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:07.160
Huh?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:09.920
Who is Lain?

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.100
Who is Lain?

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.120
Who is Lain?

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.530
There's something wrong with us!

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:23.080
We saw someone die right in front of us yesterday,

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:27.510
but we're acting like it's something we saw in a movie.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:34.310
I know we were there last night, but it didn't seem real.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.620
I guess it's like that for me, too.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:41.290
I don't think you should take it so seriously, Arisu.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.000
No, that's not what I mean.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:47.230
I'm saying it's strange that we can't take it seriously.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.720
Right, Lain?

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.100
Huh? What?

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.540
What's that, a love letter?

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.350
No way!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.360
N-No! I don't think it is, anyway...

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.940
Let us see! Let us see!

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.780
Come on, don't be stingy! Show us!

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.780
Stop that! It's mean!

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.990
A brown paper envelope, huh?

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.780
What's written on it?

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:16.470
Huh?

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:17.760
What the heck is this?

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.160
Talk about boring!

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:24.090
I knew it.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.490
Psyche...

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:15.740
You've got it all wrong! Somebody peeped into my voice mail!

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.140
I can't believe it!

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:22.090
As the relevant clauses were not in the resume we received,

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:26.680
we are currently discussing how to handle it. As for your company...

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:31.320
I love kissing. Just kissing is enough to make me happy.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:36.000
You heard about that kid pulling a stupid stunt on Accela, right?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.070
Looks like the black market supplier is freaking out.

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:41.300
You can't find it anywhere now.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:46.470
Rumor has it that the Psyche chip is mass-produced in factories in Taiwan.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:50.610
Rumor also says that it was designed by a group called the Knights.

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:55.780
But I'm not sure if these "Knights" even exist.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.280
In the Wired, there are a lot of urban legends like that.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.190
Dying feels so good!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.420
I feel accelerated...

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:08.430
What the...? There's someone in my room!

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:12.610
It's a little person like a kid in a red and green striped shirt!

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:18.440
I can't move in my bed! It's standing by my door, watching me!

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.160
Help me!

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:25.280
I have a picture of you with your secret lover.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:29.190
I just want to do business. What do you say?

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:34.350
If you don't buy it, I'll leak this image data to your company's server.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.290
You'll be famous all over the Wired.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:43.000
Lain, why won't you come here?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:54.210
Lain has new mail.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:56.780
Navi...

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.650
How's it going, Lain?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:02.370
Gotten used to your new Navi?

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.210
Something wrong?

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.960
Do you know what this is?

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.000
No.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.470
I thought...

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.230
I thought you'd know, Dad.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:32.880
I said I don't know.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:24.160
Come on, why not?

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:27.040
No... I can't...

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:30.080
Why not? I love you.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:36.940
Lain!

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:44.120
Where've you been lately? I haven't seen you around.

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.080
I...

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:51.560
What the...? Damn, you're sure going for the "little girl" look today...

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:58.160
Let's have another rave, okay? I'll leave the planning to you.

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.890
Why're you trying to act so tough?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:11.890
Excuse me.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.550
Look who's talking!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.350
Do you know what this is?

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.090
I-Is that a Psyche?!

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:29.270
Wha...

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.310
No way!

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:32.370
I've never seen one before!

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.040
W-Where did you buy it?

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:38.360
You know what this is?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.040
What're you saying?

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:46.370
With that installed, I could get full access to the Wired with even this!

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.540
How do you use it?

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:52.620
Talk about lame! You don't even know that?

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.050
Can I buy it off you? Can I?

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.660
Moron! Like you could buy something like that!

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.470
What kind of Navi do you have?

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.060
I'm not really sure. It's a Tachibana.

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:06.530
Their newest model, I think.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.160
Awesome!

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:13.540
Have you gotten inside it?

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.890
You in eighth grade? Ninth?

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:22.700
Eighth.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.490
Then you've taken Basic Information, right?

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.590
A Navi's basic motherboard layout is in the textbook.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:34.620
You connect it to the board, opposite the main processor.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:40.710
It intercepts the original data and manipulates it on its own.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.210
Using it is easier than building a model kit.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.720
You just need to watch out for static electricity.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.250
Oh. Thanks.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:52.610
Hold it!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:57.750
Information isn't free, not in the Wired or in the real world.

00:18:58.560 --> 00:19:00.730
How much you gonna charge? How much?

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:03.760
Uh...

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:06.490
You're Lain, aren't you?

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:12.790
I saw you once. In the Wired.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.290
You saw me? In the Wired?

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.770
You were totally different then than you are now.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:26.050
Most people take on a personality in the Wired

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:28.750
that's different than what they have in the real world,

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.390
but yours are total opposites.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:32.680
No way!

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:37.650
You were here when that idiot started shooting, too, weren't you?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.920
What are you planning?

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:43.110
What... What should I do for you?

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:47.170
Go out on a date with me!

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:47.970
Moron.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:51.200
But not like you are now.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.750
I want the wild Lain.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.540
I-I'm just kidding!

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:02.280
But if you feel like it sometime...

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.850
What're you talking about?!

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.190
Hey...

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.060
Forget about it! Let's go!

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:07.780
Sure!

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.290
What's so great about you?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.450
Uh... Excuse me?

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.710
Are you here to see someone?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.740
Who are you?

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:44.840
You never saw us.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.390
W-What? I'll call the police!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:53.900
We're not here, you see.

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:00.370
H-Hey...

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.500
W-What the hell?

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.320
Mom, if they show up again, call the cops!

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:17.760
Are you listening, Mom?

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:21.020
Damn it...

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:38.520
W-What're you doing, Lain?

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:52.260
What are you doing? Why are you dressed like that?

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:56.740
Well, I heard that you have to watch out for static electricity.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:22:00.890
So I thought it'd probably be safest if I took off my clothes.

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:05.310
A-Are you kidding?

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.470
Welcome home, sis!

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:35.550
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:35.550
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:39.460
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:39.460
now I am punished.

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:45.760
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:45.760
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:52.670
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:52.670
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:03.860
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:03.860
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:08.310
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:08.310
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:14.500
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:14.500
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:21.740
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:21.740
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:29.790
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:29.790
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:39.700
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:39.700
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:45.310
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:45.310
You probably don't know

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:53.020
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:53.020
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
